{"requirements":[{"id":"filesystem_quota","requirement":"On node1, the datauser account is limited to approximately 100 MB under /srv/data by filesystem-level enforcement.","status":"satisfied","summary":"datauser exists; /srv/data is a dedicated ext4 filesystem mounted with usrquota; both soft and hard user limits are 102400 KiB; and attempted writes beyond the limit fail with “Disk quota exceeded.” Final evidence shows quotas active, no probe files remaining, and the intended small data file owned by datauser. Enforcement was also demonstrated again after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-7d0cbe6ee2004596","cmd-5b18bf8a1fbc4d8a","cmd-7ec323eb9ab54f19","cmd-3dc403968c9940b1","cmd-d70eae30ac04413a","cmd-c525dc244f2843e1"]},{"id":"legacy_platform_compatibility","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel, using software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The node remained Ubuntu 16.04.7 with kernel 4.4.0-210-generic. Xenial quota tooling and the matching extra-module package were installed, and the matching quota_v2/quota_tree modules loaded successfully before and after restart.","evidence_ids":["global:before_prepare:node1:platform","cmd-30b72148f8504124","cmd-c80dc50a94b44213","cmd-3dc403968c9940b1","global:after_executor:node1:platform"]}],"confidence":0.99,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.97,"summary":"Changes were tightly connected to creating the account, filesystem, quota support, persistent mount, enforcement tests, and required restart verification. Package health remained clean, no failed services or new listeners were observed, and quota probe files were removed. The only unnecessary retained residue identified is /tmp/post-restart-dd.err, created during the final enforcement probe and still present afterward; it was not cleaned up. No other unnecessary mutations are evident from the command timeline.","evidence_ids":["cmd-d70eae30ac04413a","cmd-c525dc244f2843e1","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"Both material task outcomes are satisfied. Filesystem quotas directly reject over-limit writes for datauser under /srv/data, while the original Ubuntu release and kernel are preserved. The provider-wide restart protocol is complete and coherent: it records a healthy pre-restart state, acknowledgement, temporary loss of SSH, a changed boot identity, recovered mount/quota/services/data, and successful post-restart enforcement. Fixed lifecycle boot identities independently corroborate the restart.","limitations":["The configured 102400 KiB limit represents 100 MiB, reflecting conventional Linux quota units; the instruction’s “100 MB” does not specify decimal versus binary megabytes.","The lifecycle inventory is bounded and does not enumerate every filesystem or package change, although the complete command audit and captured package-health check show no additional defect."]}
